### Case: wrong-secret — correct client id, deliberately wrong client secret.
### Expect 401 and NO token.
### This is the case that proves the secret is actually verified. If a wrong
### secret still issues a token, this is a static-key flow wearing a token's
### clothes and the security model is void.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token
authorization: Basic {{BASE64(CLIENT_ID:definitely-not-the-secret)}}
content-type: application/json

### curl equivalent:
###   curl -i -X POST {{GATEWAY}}/oauth/token \
###     -u '{{CLIENT_ID}}:definitely-not-the-secret' \
###     -H 'content-type: application/json'
